  "description": "Headless engine behind BrixCMS — a free, open-source, block-based CMS with visual editor, AI chatbot, PDF semantic search and a full Content Delivery API.\n\n⚠️ THIS PACKAGE IS HEADLESS ONLY — no admin UI included\nThis package contains the DbContext, services, models and Content Delivery API only. It does NOT include the MVC Controllers, Razor Views or the /Manager visual admin panel — those are web-UI files that are intentionally not packed into this library. If you want the full CMS with the drag-and-drop admin panel out of the box, use the project template instead:\n\n  dotnet new install BrixCMS.Open.Templates\n  dotnet new brixcms -n MyWebsite\n\nUse BrixCMS.Open.Core directly only if you're embedding the headless engine (DbContext + services + Content API) into your own ASP.NET Core project and will build/bring your own admin UI, or will copy Areas/Controllers/Views from the GitHub repo yourself.\n\nQUICK SETUP (headless)\n  dotnet add package BrixCMS.Open.Core\n\n  // Program.cs\n  builder.Services.AddBrixCms(builder.Configuration);\n  var app = builder.Build();\n  await app.InitializeBrixCmsAsync();\n  app.MapBrixCmsApi();     // /api/content/*  — headless REST API\n  app.Run();\n\nWHAT YOU GET\n✅ 50+ content block types (Hero, Gallery, FAQ, Cards, Map, Video, QR Code, Countdown…)\n✅ Automatic page version history — restore any prior published version\n✅ AI chatbot — Ollama (local, free) or Gemini (cloud, free tier BYOK)\n✅ PDF semantic search with in-memory vector store\n✅ Headless REST API: GET /api/content/pages/{slug} returns nested block tree\n✅ Multi-admin with role-based permissions (owner / admin / member)\n✅ SQLite (zero-config) · SQL Server · PostgreSQL via EF Core 10\n✅ Newsletter subscriber API\n✅ Image optimisation (ImageSharp), QR codes, Markdown, XML Sitemap\n✅ AES-256-GCM API key encryption · TOTP 2FA · PBKDF2-SHA256 passwords\n✅ Rate limiting, CSRF, security headers out of the box\n✅ MIT license\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/Learsi23/BrixCMS\nPro / Docs: https://brixc-ms.com",
